    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d777">

                <pb facs="0864" n="854" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg854"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">093.612/49: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-29T21:00:00-04:00">March 29, 1944—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>739. Your 1046, March 25, midnight.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d777-f1"/> The War
                    Department has communicated to us its definite decision that General Connolly
                    but not General Burns is eligible for Soviet decoration and is so informing
                    General Deane. You are, therefore, authorized to inform the Soviet Government of
                    the foregoing.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d777-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d777-f1" n="27" xml:id="d777-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d777-f2" n="28" xml:id="d777-f2-content">
                <p>Ambassador Harriman informed the Foreign Commissariat of the eligibility of
                    General Connolly for a Soviet decoration on March 31, 1944.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
